# Task 65.9.1D - Docker build-context hygiene for the `./backend` build
# context. This context is used by `Dockerfile` (dev), `Dockerfile.prod`,
# and `Dockerfile.ai-base` (see `docker-compose.yml` / `docker-compose.prod.yml`
# `build.context: ./backend` and `.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml`).
# Every pattern below was checked against the actual COPY/ADD instructions
# in all three Dockerfiles, against Alembic migrations/health checks, and
# against the dev bind mount (`./backend:/app` in docker-compose.yml) before
# being added - nothing required by the build, migrations, health checks,
# `docker compose exec backend pytest ...`, or application startup is
# excluded here. Patterns use `**/` where the underlying directory/file can
# legitimately appear at any depth (e.g. `__pycache__`); patterns are kept
# bare/rooted where the item only ever exists at the context root, so a
# same-named real source path elsewhere in `app/` is never shadowed (for
# example `app/cache/` and `app/modules/media/` are real source modules and
# must never be matched by the `media/` or a hypothetical `cache/` rule
# below - verified with an isolated `docker build` reproduction before this
# file was written).

# --- Git and editor metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.fleet/
.history/

# --- Secrets and local configuration ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12

# --- Python caches and build output ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.tox/
**/.nox/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Runtime data and logs ---
**/*.log
media/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.pid

# --- Generated evaluation/benchmark artifacts (Task 65.9.1D: this
#     directory is ~110MB, git-tracked for historical record-keeping, and
#     never read by the running application - only by offline eval scripts
#     under scripts/ that default to writing here, not reading from here at
#     build/startup time) ---
artifacts/

# --- Tests: intentionally retained in this shared ignore file, not
#     excluded. The dev image (Dockerfile) is bind-mounted over by
#     `./backend:/app` at runtime (docker-compose.yml), so
#     `docker compose exec backend pytest tests/...` always sees the host
#     tree regardless of what got baked into the image at build time -
#     excluding tests/ here does not remove Dockerized test availability.
#     tests/ IS still listed below because the *production* image built
#     from the same context (Dockerfile.prod) never runs pytest and should
#     not ship a ~6MB test tree it will never execute.
tests/

# --- Task 65.9.1F.2: Celery Beat runtime-generated schedule database
#     (backend/celerybeat-schedule, created at runtime by the
#     maintenance_worker's `celery beat` process - a GNU dbm/ndbm state
#     file, never read by the build or by application startup). Bare,
#     context-relative, exact paths only - never a broad pattern.
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat-schedule.*

# --- OS temporary files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
